# aurora.local / packages/git/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/git/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/git/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>
#
# THE BIGGEST FINDING IN THIS WHOLE TASK IS IN THIS FILE — read this
# before adopting either pin below.
#
# Forgejo changed its entire versioning scheme in April 2024: v1.21 (what
# compose.yml pins today) was internally already semver v6.0, and the
# public jump to v7.0 marked Forgejo becoming a hard fork with true
# SemVer. Forgejo is now at v16.0.2 (2026-07-30) — v7 through v16 is NINE
# major-version bumps since our pinned line, each of which may carry
# breaking changes per Forgejo's own semver contract. Worse: v1.21 is not
# merely "an old major", it is dead — codeberg.org's registry shows no
# `1.21.x` tag published since 1.21.11-2 on 2024-06-13. That line will
# never receive another security fix. Forgejo v11.0 (the next LTS after
# the old scheme) reached its own end of support in July 2026, days
# before this check; the current LTS is v15.0 (supported to July 2027),
# with v16.0 the latest non-LTS stable.
#
# Judgement: this is NOT a same-major patch bump, so it is deliberately
# NOT resolved here as a routine pin. Recorded below is a digest-freeze
# of the current, EOL 1.21.11-2 — matching exactly what compose.yml
# already runs (`:1.21` has not moved since June 2024), so this is not a
# regression, but it is not "safe" either: it is a frozen, unpatched
# version. Migrating to v15.0 LTS or v16.0.2 is a real, deliberate project
# — read every RELEASE-NOTES.md from v7.0 up (config option removals,
# permission-model changes, the new runner registration flow introduced
# in v15) and test on a backup before touching a production instance.
# That migration is out of scope for this task and is not performed here.
#
# forgejo/forgejo — 1.21.11-2 (last-ever release on the pre-fork
# numbering, 2024-06-13). Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed.
IMAGE_FORGEJO=codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo:1.21.11-2@sha256:ea792343484a45f387b05540874aa0836fd0c251522f94d488f1df65faa1763e

# forgejo/runner — the runner has its OWN independent version numbering
# (3.5.1 -> 5.0.4 -> ... -> v13.0.0 as of 2026-08-03) and must be upgraded
# in step with the server, not ahead of it: runner v8.0.0 introduced
# mandatory workflow-schema validation that can silently stop older,
# loosely-written workflow files from running, and the v15-era server
# registration flow the newest runners assume does not exist on our
# frozen 1.21 server. Left at the exact version compose.yml already
# pins (3.5.1) rather than "upgraded" independently — moving it without
# also completing the server migration above would be a worse mismatch
# than leaving both alone. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_FORGEJO_RUNNER=code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner:3.5.1@sha256:173389594aeb4a7681ba073edf0498282cf301fe13c72b751f264e198010f3d1
